<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Rashiq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Rashiq was an officer of the poet-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-ammar">Ibn Ammar</a> who took over the rule of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a> in the early 1080s, defying al-Mutamid of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>. His dealings with the Castilian garrison at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aledo">Aledo</a> made him unpopular, and after the Almoravid siege of Aledo in 1088 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a> handed him over to al-Mutamid, ending his rule.</p></div>
